&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will support one of Pinterest’s most strategic businesses in LATAM, partnering closely on the &lt;strong&gt;Mercado Libre business across Hispanic markets&lt;/strong&gt;. You will help advertisers get the most out of Pinterest by driving strong campaign execution, performance optimization, measurement rigor, and clear client communication. You’ll collaborate closely with sales and cross-functional teams while helping bring structure, insights, and momentum to a complex regional account.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and nurture strong relationships with partners by proactively communicating on campaign performance, optimizations, updates, and growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Client Partner to support a complex regional business across multiple Hispanic LATAM markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure partner objectives and requirements are met by coordinating effectively with internal teams including Measurement, Product Marketing, Creative Strategy, Performance Solutions, and others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain a deep understanding of partner business goals and turn data into compelling stories and actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the “how” conversation with advertisers by advising on targeting, bidding, creative, measurement, pacing, and optimization approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert in Pinterest campaign best practices and performance solutions, and act as a trusted resource on performance-related opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure campaign setup and execution are strong, monitor results closely, troubleshoot issues, and take action to course-correct when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpret and communicate campaign results clearly so that partners understand impact, opportunity, and next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support QBRs, performance recaps, and other business reviews with strong analysis and clear recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively participate in client meetings, helping explain complex solutions in a simple, credible, and commercially relevant way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle resistance, objections, and product questions thoughtfully and professionally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify cross-sell and upsell opportunities that can contribute to account growth and team revenue goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong fluency in Pinterest ad products, performance solutions, and evolving roadmap updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner efficiently with cross-functional teams to resolve issues, answer technical questions, and support business growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pitch new performance products and best practices at scale where relevant&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in digital advertising, account management, or media with responsibility for campaign performance and client communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of turning data into compelling recommendations and business actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex workstreams, stakeholders, and deadlines with strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of campaign optimization, performance measurement, attribution, and analytical problem-solving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with technical and performance-oriented media solutions, including areas such as tagging, measurement, analytics, shopping, search, display, paid social, or lower-funnel advertising&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate clearly and effectively in person, on the phone, and in writing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work cross-functionally with both technical and non-technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sense of ownership, accountability, and follow-through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a fast-paced environment with ambiguity and shifting priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing sophisticated client or agency relationships is strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field such as math, economics, marketing, business, engineering, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relocation Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
