&lt;li&gt;Execute scoped technical tasks end-to-end to help build the future of Pinterest&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver code that is well-documented, tested, and operable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage &lt;strong&gt;AI tools&lt;/strong&gt; in your daily engineering workflow to accelerate delivery—brainstorming approaches, writing and refining code, and producing clear documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate ideas and perspectives with candor as you grow professionally through learning and development opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with your team and contribute to real projects that impact Pinterest&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engage with&lt;/strong&gt; leaders and employees across Pinterest and &lt;strong&gt;participate in&lt;/strong&gt; a variety of optional company events&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Currently enrolled&lt;/strong&gt; in a degree or education program working toward a Bachelor’s or Master’s in Computer Science or a related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On track to graduate by &lt;strong&gt;June 2029&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to demonstrate an understanding of computer science fundamentals, including data structures and algorithms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity using &lt;strong&gt;AI as a learning, productivity, &lt;/strong&gt;and&lt;strong&gt; engineering tool&lt;/strong&gt;, and as an iterative coding partner, to accelerate engineering work while exercising strong judgment around accuracy, security, and when to ask for help&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with one or more programming languages such as Python, Java, JavaScript/TypeScript, Go, or C++, and familiarity with relevant frameworks, tools, or technologies such as React or similar. Technical requirements vary by team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Non-academic coding experience (e.g., &lt;strong&gt;hackathons&lt;/strong&gt;, code challenges, personal projects, GitHub, open source, volunteer coding experience, conference participation, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for Pinterest, comfort with ambiguity, and a growth mindset with a willingness to continuously learn&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
