&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progressive HR experience, including substantial experience as an HR Business Partner supporting senior leaders in complex, matrixed organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting regional or international teams across multiple countries and cultures, ideally within APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong track record advising senior leaders on talent strategy, organizational effectiveness, leadership development, change and employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with sales, revenue or other fast-paced commercial organizations is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen with the ability to connect People strategy to business outcomes and influence decisions through clear, data-informed insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in talent management, organization design, change leadership and leadership coaching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent judgment, discretion and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to build trust and influence across functions and levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and AI fluency, including experience using AI to improve speed and quality while validating accuracy, protecting sensitive data and remaining accountable for final decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of employment practices and the ability to navigate varied regional contexts, including effective partnership with Singapore’s Ministry of Manpower and Economic Development Board.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration or a related field, or equivalent experience. Advanced HR or business credentials are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A resilient, adaptable and inclusive leadership style, with the ability to operate calmly through ambiguity, complexity and change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
