&lt;p&gt;What you’ll do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the technical vision and multi-year roadmap for the Notifications &amp;amp; Growth Platform org, aligning architecture and execution plans to Pinterest’s engagement and retention goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional delivery of end-to-end solutions by partnering with Product, Data Science, Design, and engineering teams to ship notifications, in-app growth experiences, and internationalized (i18n) experiences for global markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make durable architectural decisions that improve delivery quality, reliability, and scalability of Pinterest’s notifications and growth systems (e.g., orchestration, targeting hooks, scheduling, and multi-channel delivery).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success metrics and operating cadence (e.g., engagement lift, delivery success, latency, reliability, cost, adoption) and drive measurable improvements aligned to org OKRs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI to accelerate your work across exploration, drafting, analysis, and synthesis—while maintaining strong judgment, rigorous validation, and accountability for outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;What we’re looking for:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of software engineering experience, including meaningful time as a Staff, Senior Staff, or equivalent-level IC building and operating complex production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or partnering on ML-, AI-, or GenAI-adjacent systems, with a pragmatic understanding of where these technologies add value and how to deploy them responsibly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven technical leadership: driving architecture across multiple services/teams and delivering org-critical initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and ability to influence across technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Notifications and growth platform experience is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to dive into data and identify opportunities to drive user growth is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, a related field, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
