&lt;li&gt;Drive Growth ML model improvements through AB test driven innovation loop - from ideation to production launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the health of our ML ecosystem: training pipelines, feature and serving infrastructure, evaluation frameworks and monitoring, AB test set up, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help raise the technical excellence bar through mentorship, reviews, evaluations, documentation, standard setting, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate and build strong working relationships with colleagues and stakeholders to tackle big, cross-functional, initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with other engineering leaders to form technical directions and roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate autonomously, take ownership in complex and evolving environments and drive work effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and apply relevant state-of-the-art techniques from recent research and/or collaborate on novel research directions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously optimize various parts of work by building and using cutting-edge AI tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Graduate degree in Computer Science or in a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 8 years of experience in machine learning engineering, including hands-on experience building and shipping models for a large-scale, real-time, end-user production recommender system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in recommender modeling, including sequence modeling of user behavior with transformer architectures, DNN rankers and generative and LLM-native recommenders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in building and operating high-QPS, latency-constrained ML systems, including training and serving infrastructure, and in owning the cost, latency and reliability tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in industry-grade software engineering that others use as the example, and in conducting thorough code and design reviews that raise the quality of a team&#39;s work&lt;/li&gt;
